ized. The primary methods for VLAN tagging include ISL and the widely adopted 802.1Q standard [Data: Entities (1652, 2710), Relationships (3779,+more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Enhanced Network Security through VLANs\",\n            \"explanation\": \"One of the primary advantages of implementing VLANs is the significant improvement in network security. By isolating traffic between different network segments, VLANs restrict unauthorized access. For instance, sensitive server traffic can be placed on a dedicated VLAN, protected from general network access. This segmentation prevents devices in one VLAN from communicating directly with devices in another without passing through a router, which can enforce security policies. This makes it harder for threats to propagate across the entire network [Data: Entities (1652, 2686), Relationships (3725,+more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Improved Scalability and Network Management\",\n            \"explanation\": \"VLANs contribute significantly to network scalability and management. They allow networks to grow and adapt to increasing demands without requiring a complete overhaul of the physical infrastructure. Network administrators can easily add or move devices to different logical networks without reconfiguring physical cabling. This logical organization simplifies network management, enabling administrators to group devices by department or function, regardless of their physical location. This flexibility is key to supporting dynamic business environments and ensuring efficient resource utilization [Data: Entities (1652, 2685, 2687), Relationships (3726,+more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Inter-VLAN Communication Requires Routing\",\n            \"explanation\": \"While VLANs effectively segment networks and isolate broadcast traffic, communication between devices on different VLANs necessitates the use of a router. Each VLAN functions as a s